  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">TB Local Organizations Network (LON)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">(India):  .This implementing mechanism is aligned with India&apos;s National Strategic Plan (NSP) and emphasizes a comprehensive Detect-Treat-Prevent-Build approach.  It includes key activities designed to create advocates for rights-based TB care, establish community-owned monitoring mechanisms, and demonstrate gender and age responsive, stigma free TB care to TB patients...  .With FY 2021 funds, it will support community driven efforts to achieve the ambitious goal of ending TB by 2025, which necessitates a paradigm shift in approach and strategy.  It will leverage community action to build a culture of accountability and strengthen the community response to TB by engaging TB survivors as &apos;TB Champions&apos; and advocating for increased resources for TB by involving industries, elected representatives, the media, and others. The IM will conduct training of TB survivors on a right based approach to TB care, develop job aids to support TB survivors to discharge their responsibilities and conduct capacity building programs for the network of TB survivors. Deploying a rights-responsibilities framework to enhance behavior change, the project will support the national program by enabling communities to amplify the reach and effectiveness of TB prevention and care, based on the key accountability principles of integrity, inclusivity, effectiveness, and actionability.  It will provide solutions that strengthen the enabling environment to help translate commitments into action and bridge the gap between the demand and supply of TB services. This mechanism will conduct training and support TB champions and health workers on implementation of community accountability framework...These interventions support USAID&apos;s contribution to the UN target of treating 40 million people between 2018 and 2022. ..</narrative>
  </description>
